A1 -- FLAT SPACE: energy and momentum are transported at DIFFERENT rates (Noether, on-shell)
================================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1-1  energy conservation d_t(u K_u - K + c_Y w^2) + d_x(-2 c_Y u w) = 0 holds ON-SHELL (residual is exactly EOM * chi_t)   (residual = 0)
  [PASS] A1-2  momentum conservation d_t(-K_u w) + d_x(...) = 0 holds ON-SHELL (residual is exactly EOM * chi_x)   (residual = 0)
  energy density   = c_Y*Derivative(chi(t, x), x)**2 - K(Derivative(chi(t, x), t)) + Derivative(K(Derivative(chi(t, x), t)), Derivative(chi(t, x), t))*Derivative(chi(t, x), t)
  energy flux      = -2*c_Y*Derivative(chi(t, x), t)*Derivative(chi(t, x), x)
  momentum density = -Derivative(K(Derivative(chi(t, x), t)), Derivative(chi(t, x), t))*Derivative(chi(t, x), x)
  energy flux / momentum density = 2*c_Y*Derivative(chi(t, x), t)/Derivative(K(Derivative(chi(t, x), t)), Derivative(chi(t, x), t))
  [PASS] A1-3  the ratio (energy flux)/(momentum density) is 2 c_Y Q / K_Q(Q): T^{0i} != T^{i0} -- energy and momentum move at different speeds unless c_Y = K_Q/(2Q)   (ratio = 2*Q*c_Y/Derivative(K(Q), Q))
  [PASS] A1-4  CONTROL: for a Lorentz-invariant k-essence P(X), X = (u^2 - w^2)/2, i.e. K = P(u^2/2) and c_Y = P_X/2, the ratio is exactly 1 (symmetric T^{mu nu}); the mismatch IS the Lorentz violation   (ratio_LI = 1)

