A2 -- GRAVITY THROUGH THE LAPSE: the sector falls with acceleration -eps grad(Phi), eps = 2 c_Y Qbar/K_Q
================================================================================================================
  O(eps) field equation : -K_QQ*Qbar*Derivative(Phi(t, x), t) + K_QQ*Derivative(psi(t, x), (t, 2)) - 2*c_Y*Derivative(psi(t, x), (x, 2)) = 0
  delta n               : -K_QQ*Qbar*Phi(t, x) + K_QQ*Derivative(psi(t, x), t)
  [PASS] A2-1  the linearised density equation is  d_t^2(dn) - (2 c_Y/K_QQ) d_x^2(dn) = 2 c_Y Qbar d_x^2(Phi): sound speed c_s^2 = 2 c_Y/K_QQ (L138's) AND a gravitational source with coefficient 2 c_Y Qbar   (residual = 0)
  [PASS] A2-2  dividing by the background density Qbar K_Q: the source is eps * rho_bar lap(Phi) with eps = 2 c_Y Qbar/K_Q -- the sector's INERTIAL response to gravity is eps times its GRAVITATIONAL mass   (eps = 2*Qbar*c_Y/K_Q)
  [PASS] A2-3  IDENTITY for any K and any c_Y:  c_s^2 = eps * c_ad^2,  c_ad^2 = K_Q/(Qbar K_QQ) = dP/drho of the background.  A 'free' sound speed is bought with a non-universal gravitational coupling.   (c_s^2 - eps c_ad^2 = 0)
  [PASS] A2-4  eps = 1 (equivalence principle in the dark sector, the condition for CDM-like infall) FORCES c_Y = K_Q/(2 Qbar) -- the Lorentz-invariant k-essence value of A1-4 -- and hence c_s = c_ad: the sound speed is then LOCKED to the background equation of state (L138 B2), not free   (c_Y(eps=1) = K_Q/(2*Qbar))

